    description: "FOUND 2026-10-24 by WI-dipim's new advisory check (\"a kind=file id is exactly 1-1:file:file\"). json_config and toml_config mint kind=\"file\" symbols that are not file pseudo-symbols: `json:examples/addon.node/package.json:5-5:addon.node:file` (an npm `bin` / main entry), `toml:tools/distrib/python/grpcio_tools/pyproject.toml:43-43:python-grpc-tools-protoc:file` (a pyproject script). whisper.cpp 2-4, grpc 1. kind=file is reserved for the file pseudo-symbol (make_file_id). These are declarations IN a manifest that name an entry point. FIX: give them a kind that says so (the WI-bufar-pokam build-target vocabulary, or the existing defines_target edge to make_manifest_target_dst), and check what consumers of kind=file (file anchors, slices) assumed. Acceptance: 0 file-triple advisories on those surveys; then promote the check to error."  # aa56
